  "kernel_exact_rgba_pixels": 262144,
  "interpretation": "Original procedural inputs were recalculated and saved by Photoshop through its native UI. Independent Python decoding extracted expected stored samples. Integer cases use encoded RGB; raw RGB32 samples are linear. This does not certify full merge or application parity.",
  "semantics": [
    "Merge Down retains the immediate visible lower layer name; hidden lower layer disables the operation.",
    "Merge Layers retains top selected visible name and off-canvas content; selected hidden layers are removed.",
    "Merge Visible clips to the canvas and replaces active visible layer, preserving hidden layers and their order.",
    "Flatten requires distinct Background semantics and confirmation when hidden layers exist; remains unimplemented."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Full Photoshop parity remains false.",
    "Only root-level unlocked Normal raster layers without masks, transforms, clipping or groups can merge.",
    "Entirely transparent merge results remain unsupported; arbitrary hidden-active and lock contexts need qualification.",
    "All-depth kernel samples match, but native RGB32 encoded/linear transfer is not bit-reversible. Workflow RGB32 checks qualify alpha and bounded color error, not byte-identical RGB.",
    "The general renderer still uses its previous compositing arithmetic; only merge transactions use the newly measured kernel.",
    "Additional blends, groups, masks, clipping, color management, fill opacity, locks, Background and Flatten Image remain pending.",
    "Pixel selection retention is a native invariant; Photoshop selection/history behavior needs independent qualification.",
    "Intel/macOS14/macOS26 execution is not qualified on this host."
  ],
